module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.extra_source_root_outside_workspace_refuses_annotations_as_unattached

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data extra_source_root_outside_workspace_refuses_annotations_as_unattached: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "extra_source_root_outside_workspace_refuses_annotations_as_unattached" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an extra --source-root outside process_workspace_root refuses every content-carrying annotation as UnattachedAtScopeEnd, so the diagnostic names the file and conceals the invocation** (INVALID STATE: `std.source_annotation` `annotation_attach_resolve` drops a leading `//` whose text is empty when no module-item subject follows, and refuses every text-bearing line as UnattachedAtScopeEnd. That rule is content-shaped. When the extra root is not under the process workspace, the binder reports that class for every text-bearing line in the file even when a module item immediately follows the block.",

    "HARM: a composed-root consumer (private CI: `--source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root ../dag` from inside a public checkout) reads 175 corpus defects in `strategy.year_end_plan` and starts a prose migration. The file is fine under an in-workspace extra root of the same bytes. The lie is located: the diagnostic points at year_end_plan.dag:N:1, not at the source-root that was outside the workspace. Bare `//` lines 'pass' only because empty text with no following subject is a no-op, which is how the 175/12 split was misread as a placement rule.",

    "RECEIPT (2026-09-10): gunbc-private witnesses run 34451871767, public SHA 0d6b6653e0f, entry `../dag/test/claim/year_end_plan_witness_test.dag`. Discriminator, same compiler, same year_end_plan bytes: `--source-root _priv_yep` (under the workspace) and a copy under `dag/` both admit the annotations and run `year_end_plan_witness_main` to ExitSuccess; CI's `../dag` extra root from `cd public` refuses. Absolute extra root is a sibling class (`absolute_extra_source_root_panics_instead_of_typed_refusal`).",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the refusal is typed and located, but it locates the wrong subject, so harm is contained only if a reader already knows to distrust UnattachedAtScopeEnd on an extra-root file.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed once an extra source root that is not under process_workspace_root either admits annotation attachment for its files or refuses the ROOT with a typed cause naming the workspace boundary before any per-line UnattachedAtScopeEnd is emitted.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: extra `--source-root` directories outside process_workspace_root are either admitted for module-scope annotation attachment on the same terms as an in-workspace extra root, or refused as a root with a diagnostic that names the workspace boundary -- sufficient for a composed-root consumer to stop seeing UnattachedAtScopeEnd on a file that attaches under an in-workspace copy of the same bytes. A private overlay copy into the public checkout CONTRIBUTES to living with the class and does not retire it.)",

    "STANDING AFTER parse-comment-gap-attachment (2026-10-12, gunbc#13754): THE REFUSAL ARM IS GONE, THE CLASS IS NOT SHOWN DISSOLVED. std.source_annotation attach_annotations now places every capture in a gap (scope = innermost retained region containing it, the file when none does), so UnattachedAtScopeEnd and annotation_attach_resolve no longer exist and an extra-root file no longer refuses. What made an out-of-workspace root's files find no following item was never identified. If that cause persists it now shows a different shape: an empty or mis-keyed region roster attaches each comment to FileScope with no neighbours, silently -- below the ladder, where the false refusal at least stopped the line. It is UNVERIFIED either way: no consumer outside v1.tests.claim.annotation_gap_round_trip_test reads the attachment graph today, so nothing can observe a wrong gap on this path. NEXT TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the first consumer that reads gaps for a composed-root file runs this row's discriminator -- the same bytes under an in-workspace and an out-of-workspace extra root must bind identical structural gap keys (v1.compiler.annotation_bind keyed_annotation_rows) -- and refuses the root with a typed cause naming the workspace boundary where they differ. Until then this row stays open at its new shape.",

    "DISSOLVED (2026-10-12), BY AN ENROLLED DISCRIMINATOR, superseding the UNVERIFIED standing above. The control is v1.tests.claim.extra_root_annotation_gap_agreement_test: it binds the same source bytes -- comments above a data row, above a fn, inside the body and trailing a statement -- through the compile frontend's per-file calls (tokenize_artifact, parse_with_table_in_occurrence_scope, v1.compiler.annotation_bind bind_annotations and keyed_annotation_rows), once under an in-workspace path spelling and once under an out-of-workspace one. in_and_out_of_workspace_roots_bind_identical_gaps_holds requires their structural gap keys to agree; a_moved_comment_disagrees_across_roots_holds shows the comparison fails when a comment moves. The path the original receipt was observed on, `gunbc run`, resolves through the via-index parse cache, which parse-comment-gap-attachment (gunbc#13754) stopped binding annotations on, so it can neither refuse nor mis-attach. The original cause was NOT identified: the refusal arm and the via-index binding that produced it are gone, and the remaining binding route agrees across root spellings. Reopen when that control fails, or when any composed-root file's structural gap keys differ between an in- and out-of-workspace copy of the same bytes.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.tests.claim.extra_root_annotation_gap_agreement_test", decl_name: "in_and_out_of_workspace_roots_bind_identical_gaps_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.tests.claim.extra_root_annotation_gap_agreement_test", decl_name: "a_moved_comment_disagrees_across_roots_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
